4. INTELLIGENT FILE CLASSIFICATION

For every file, determine its most likely category using:

- Filename
- Extension
- File metadata
- Creation date
- Modification date
- File location
- Folder context
- Document contents where permitted
- Sender/source where available
- Related files
- Naming patterns

Examples:

"Aadhaar.pdf"
→ Documents / Government / Identity

"SBI_Statement_Aug_2026.pdf"
→ Documents / Banking & Finance / Statements

"Property_Sale_Deed.pdf"
→ Documents / Property / Legal

"Invoice_12345.pdf"
→ Documents / Receipts & Invoices

"IMG_20260920.jpg"
→ Media / Photos

"Screen_Recording_2026.mp4"
→ Media / Screen Recordings

Do not rely solely on filenames when the context suggests otherwise.

---

5. DUPLICATE DETECTION

Identify duplicates using:

- Exact file hash
- File size
- Filename
- Content similarity
- Image similarity where available
- Document similarity

Separate duplicates into:

DEFINITE DUPLICATES

Identical files.

PROBABLE DUPLICATES

Nearly identical files requiring review.

RELATED BUT DIFFERENT

Versions of the same document that may contain different information.

Never delete duplicates automatically.

For potentially important documents, preserve the newest and/or most complete version and place other copies into a review/archive area only after confirmation.

